  <title>Cat FAQ</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      color-scheme: light;
      --bg: #f7f8fc;
      --card: #ffffff;
      --text: #172033;
      --muted: #657086;
      --line: #e7eaf2;
      --accent: #6c5ce7;
      --accent-soft: #efedff;
      --shadow: 0 24px 70px rgba(32, 41, 71, 0.12);
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      min-height: 100vh;
      font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
      color: var(--text);
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at top left, rgba(108, 92, 231, 0.18), transparent 32rem),
        linear-gradient(135deg, #fbfcff 0%, var(--bg) 100%);
    }

    main {
      width: min(920px, calc(100% - 32px));
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 72px 0;
    }

    .hero {
      margin-bottom: 32px;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      margin-bottom: 16px;
      padding: 8px 12px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(108, 92, 231, 0.22);
      border-radius: 999px;
      color: var(--accent);
      background: var(--accent-soft);
      font-size: 0.86rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    }

    h1 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
      line-height: 0.98;
      letter-spacing: -0.06em;
    }

    .intro {
      max-width: 620px;
      margin: 18px auto 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 1.08rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .faq-card {
      overflow: hidden;
      border: 1px solid rgba(231, 234, 242, 0.9);
      border-radius: 28px;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.84);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
      backdrop-filter: blur(18px);
    }

    .example + .example {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    }

    .question {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      width: 100%;
      gap: 24px;
      padding: 26px 28px;
      border: 0;
      color: inherit;
      background: transparent;
      font: inherit;
      font-size: 1.08rem;
      font-weight: 760;
      text-align: left;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    .question:hover,
    .question:focus-visible {
      background: rgba(108, 92, 231, 0.055);
    }

    .question:focus-visible {
      outline: 3px solid rgba(108, 92, 231, 0.32);
      outline-offset: -3px;
    }

    .icon {
      display: grid;
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      width: 34px;
      height: 34px;
      place-items: center;
      border-radius: 12px;
      color: var(--accent);
      background: var(--accent-soft);
      transition: transform 180ms ease, background 180ms ease;
    }

    .icon::before,
    .icon::after {
      grid-area: 1 / 1;
      width: 14px;
      height: 2px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: currentColor;
      content: "";
      transition: transform 180ms ease;
    }

    .icon::after {
      transform: rotate(90deg);
    }

    .question[aria-expanded="true"] .icon {
      background: #e4e0ff;
      transform: rotate(180deg);
    }

    .question[aria-expanded="true"] .icon::after {
      transform: rotate(0deg);
    }

    .details {
      padding: 0 28px 28px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 1rem;
      line-height: 1.75;
    }

    .details[hidden] {
      display: none;
    }

    .details p {
      max-width: 720px;
      margin: 0;
    }

    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      main {
        width: min(100% - 20px, 920px);
        padding: 40px 0;
      }

      .faq-card {
        border-radius: 22px;
      }

      .question {
        padding: 22px 20px;
        font-size: 1rem;
      }

      .details {
        padding: 0 20px 24px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
      <div class="eyebrow">Cat care basics</div>
      <h1 id="page-title">FAQ for curious cat people</h1>
      <p class="intro">Quick answers to common questions about happy, healthy indoor cats. Select a question to expand the answer.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="faq-card" aria-label="Frequently asked questions about cats">
      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-1" id="question-1">
          Why do cats purr?
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-1" hidden>
          <p>Cats often purr when they feel relaxed or content, but purring can also happen when they are seeking comfort, recovering, or communicating with people and other cats.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-2" id="question-2">
          How much sleep do cats need?
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-2" hidden>
          <p>Most adult cats sleep 12 to 16 hours a day. Kittens and senior cats may sleep even more, especially after play, meals, or periods of exploration.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-3" id="question-3">
          Why does my cat knead blankets or laps?
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-3" hidden>
          <p>Kneading is a comforting behavior that begins in kittenhood. Adult cats may knead soft surfaces when they feel safe, affectionate, or ready to settle in for a nap.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-4" id="question-4">
          What should an indoor cat have at home?
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-4" hidden>
          <p>Indoor cats benefit from fresh water, nutritious food, clean litter, cozy resting spots, scratching surfaces, climbing space, window views, toys, and regular interactive play.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-5" id="question-5">
          How can I tell if my cat is stressed?
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-5" hidden>
          <p>Stress signs can include hiding, reduced appetite, overgrooming, litter box changes, flattened ears, tail flicking, or sudden aggression. Persistent changes are a good reason to contact a veterinarian.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    const questions = document.querySelectorAll(".question");

    questions.forEach((question) => {
      question.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const answer = document.getElementById(question.getAttribute("aria-controls"));
        const isExpanded = question.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";

        question.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isExpanded));
        answer.hidden = isExpanded;
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
