           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="answer-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-2" hidden>
           <p>Most adult cats sleep 12 to 16 hours a day. Kittens and senior cats may sleep even more, especially after play, meals, or periods of exploration.</p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-3" id="question-3">
           Why does my cat knead blankets or laps?
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="answer-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-3" hidden>
           <p>Kneading is a comforting behavior that begins in kittenhood. Adult cats may knead soft surfaces when they feel safe, affectionate, or ready to settle in for a nap.</p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-4" id="question-4">
           What should an indoor cat have at home?
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
