         </button>
         <div class="details" id="answer-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-5" hidden>
           <p>Stress signs can include hiding, reduced appetite, overgrooming, litter box changes, flattened ears, tail flicking, or sudden aggression. Persistent changes are a good reason to contact a veterinarian.</p>
